1
00:00:04,933 --> 00:00:11,933
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:38,367 --> 00:00:40,167
[SCREAMING IN PAIN]

3
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:42,867
[TIRES SCREECHING]

4
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:46,667
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:55,367 --> 00:00:57,367
[TIRES SCREECH]

6
00:00:57,367 --> 00:00:59,400
[ENGINES REVVING]

7
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:00,733
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

8
00:01:00,733 --> 00:01:02,100
[LOUD CRASH]

9
00:01:02,100 --> 00:01:04,100
[TIRES SCREECHING]

10
00:01:05,333 --> 00:01:07,100
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOTS]</i>

11
00:01:10,233 --> 00:01:12,633
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

12
00:01:12,633 --> 00:01:16,767
[METAL RODS CLANGING]

13
00:01:16,767 --> 00:01:19,133
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

14
00:01:20,067 --> 00:01:21,633
[GLASS SHATTERING]

15
00:01:21,633 --> 00:01:23,900
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

16
00:01:25,133 --> 00:01:28,333
[ENGINES REVVING]

17
00:01:30,067 --> 00:01:31,500
[TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:33,033 --> 00:01:34,833
[TIRES SCREECHING]

19
00:01:34,833 --> 00:01:36,167
[GUNSHOTS]

20
00:01:36,167 --> 00:01:37,267
[TIRES SCREECHING]

21
00:01:37,267 --> 00:01:38,967
- [TRUCK HORN HONKS]
- [LOUD CRASH]

22
00:01:38,967 --> 00:01:40,500
[TIRES SCREECHING]

23
00:01:45,300 --> 00:01:48,167
<i>Aren't you supposed
to ambush the reporter today?</i>

24
00:01:48,167 --> 00:01:49,667
<i> That's already taken care of.</i>

25
00:01:49,667 --> 00:01:51,300
<i> If we mess up this job,</i>

26
00:01:51,300 --> 00:01:53,567
<i>we're going to lose
a lot of money!</i>

27
00:01:53,567 --> 00:01:54,767
<i> So, do a good job!</i>

28
00:01:54,767 --> 00:01:56,467
<i> I'll get back at them, Ma.</i>

29
00:01:56,467 --> 00:01:58,067
<i>Our men will take care
of it.</i>

30
00:01:58,067 --> 00:02:00,433
<i>I'm not talking
about Mr. Chan, Ma.</i>

31
00:02:00,433 --> 00:02:02,133
<i> The one who shot me!</i>

32
00:02:02,133 --> 00:02:04,033
<i>You arrested him
without a warrant.</i>

33
00:02:04,033 --> 00:02:06,733
<i>Unless Mr. Chan agrees
to cooperate with us.</i>

34
00:02:06,733 --> 00:02:08,233
<i> I'll make him confess.</i>

35
00:02:08,233 --> 00:02:10,033
<i>How are you connected
with Victor Zafra?</i>

36
00:02:10,033 --> 00:02:13,433
<i> I will not tell you.</i>

37
00:02:13,433 --> 00:02:15,333
<i>We can even
lighten your sentence.</i>

38
00:02:15,367 --> 00:02:18,067
You are very desperate already.

39
00:02:18,067 --> 00:02:20,533
<i>When I'm asking you,
you better answer properly!</i>

40
00:02:20,533 --> 00:02:21,967
- [SPITS]
- [BLOW LANDS]

41
00:02:21,967 --> 00:02:23,967
<i>- Jacinto!
- She hit me!</i>

42
00:02:23,967 --> 00:02:27,367
<i>That gold is the reason
we lost everything.</i>

43
00:02:27,367 --> 00:02:28,733
<i>- Ugh!
- Aah!</i>

44
00:02:28,733 --> 00:02:30,067
<i> I'm begging you.</i>

45
00:02:30,067 --> 00:02:32,867
<i>We haven't received justice
for what they did to my mother.</i>

46
00:02:32,867 --> 00:02:36,467
<i>Those cops caused me
so much suffering.</i>

47
00:02:36,467 --> 00:02:39,233
<i>I swear I will find out
who they are.</i>

48
00:02:39,233 --> 00:02:40,767
<i> I will hunt them down</i>

49
00:02:40,767 --> 00:02:43,633
<i>and destroy them
and their families.</i>

50
00:02:45,667 --> 00:02:46,633
[RUDY GRUNTS]

51
00:02:46,633 --> 00:02:48,000
Take it easy.

52
00:02:50,467 --> 00:02:51,667
Gabo.

53
00:02:51,667 --> 00:02:53,033
Come on, let's go home.

54
00:02:54,867 --> 00:02:55,833
Okay, Pa.

55
00:02:57,400 --> 00:02:58,667
How's the motorcycle?

56
00:02:59,500 --> 00:03:01,833
Uh... I got it already, Pa.

57
00:03:01,833 --> 00:03:03,200
It's working fine.

58
00:03:04,700 --> 00:03:06,800
Alright then. You go ahead.

59
00:03:07,433 --> 00:03:09,667
Okay, I'll just get
the motorcycle.

60
00:03:11,700 --> 00:03:13,833
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

61
00:03:13,833 --> 00:03:16,067
[RUDY] I'm really proud
of my son.

62
00:03:17,433 --> 00:03:21,133
He found a way to get
money for my surgery.

63
00:03:21,167 --> 00:03:22,567
Yeah, yeah. Fine.
Come on.

64
00:03:22,567 --> 00:03:24,133
We're going to get stuck
in traffic.

65
00:03:24,833 --> 00:03:27,633
- Let's go.
- [MAMENG] Take it easy, okay?

66
00:03:27,633 --> 00:03:30,033
- You good?
- [MAMENG] Don't rush it.

67
00:03:30,033 --> 00:03:36,500
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

68
00:03:37,633 --> 00:03:39,867
Okay. You know what to do.

69
00:03:39,867 --> 00:03:41,733
This is an easy job, right?

70
00:03:41,733 --> 00:03:44,133
- You got this.
- Leave it to us, boss.

71
00:03:44,867 --> 00:03:47,767
Just follow all the
instructions I gave you.

72
00:03:47,767 --> 00:03:50,267
- We won't fail you, boss.
- As you should.

73
00:03:52,767 --> 00:03:54,533
Make sure you
do the job right.

74
00:03:55,500 --> 00:03:59,233
If you fail,
I'll put you all down.

75
00:04:00,133 --> 00:04:02,133
Here. Now, go.

76
00:04:02,133 --> 00:04:03,200
Okay, boss.

77
00:04:03,200 --> 00:04:06,533
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

78
00:04:06,533 --> 00:04:09,133
Udo, go buy more beer.

79
00:04:09,133 --> 00:04:10,100
Yes, boss.

80
00:04:11,633 --> 00:04:18,600
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

81
00:04:20,067 --> 00:04:21,133
Sam.

82
00:04:24,667 --> 00:04:26,933
"Preventive Suspension Order"

83
00:04:26,933 --> 00:04:30,033
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

84
00:04:30,067 --> 00:04:32,267
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

85
00:04:32,267 --> 00:04:33,300
[DOOR OPENS]

86
00:04:34,467 --> 00:04:36,067
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

87
00:04:38,167 --> 00:04:39,167
Come in.

88
00:04:43,833 --> 00:04:45,500
Go back to work.

89
00:04:46,133 --> 00:04:47,200
Now!

90
00:04:49,667 --> 00:04:51,033
Let's talk.

91
00:04:52,200 --> 00:04:59,233
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

92
00:04:59,233 --> 00:05:00,433
[SEBASTIAN EXHALES SHARPLY]

93
00:05:01,500 --> 00:05:03,533
Why were you at
the interrogation room?

94
00:05:03,533 --> 00:05:06,400
What if you also get sanctioned
for Jacinto's violations?

95
00:05:08,133 --> 00:05:09,800
I want to protect her.

96
00:05:11,600 --> 00:05:12,667
Hmm.

97
00:05:14,733 --> 00:05:17,633
Who's going to protect you, hm?

98
00:05:17,633 --> 00:05:19,733
[EXHALES HEAVILY]

99
00:05:19,733 --> 00:05:22,333
Come on, Seb...

100
00:05:22,333 --> 00:05:25,800
You guarded your reputation
for so long.

101
00:05:25,800 --> 00:05:32,000
One mistake could erase
all your achievements.

102
00:05:35,033 --> 00:05:38,700
If I were you...

103
00:05:41,200 --> 00:05:47,467
I'd stay away from people
who ignore protocol.

104
00:05:47,467 --> 00:05:49,833
You might get dragged down
with them.

105
00:05:50,933 --> 00:05:52,733
Just saying.

106
00:05:55,233 --> 00:05:59,333
You're one of my most
trusted agents here.

107
00:06:00,300 --> 00:06:03,600
Smart. Disciplined.

108
00:06:03,600 --> 00:06:08,500
I taught you to obey the law,
not your emotions.

109
00:06:08,533 --> 00:06:10,867
But you're doing
the exact opposite.

110
00:06:12,900 --> 00:06:14,533
I'm sorry.

111
00:06:14,533 --> 00:06:18,333
I'm trying to protect
and defend you.

112
00:06:18,333 --> 00:06:23,167
But with what you're doing,
you're destroying yourself.

113
00:06:23,167 --> 00:06:25,933
First, you disobeyed me.

114
00:06:25,933 --> 00:06:29,100
Second, you charged in
on Mr. Chan

115
00:06:29,100 --> 00:06:33,333
and put your team's lives
in danger!

116
00:06:33,333 --> 00:06:40,067
Now you're interrogating
without due process?

117
00:06:40,067 --> 00:06:45,133
And you even hurt
our potential witness!

118
00:06:52,833 --> 00:06:54,767
- [GATE OPENS]
- [MR. CHAN GRUNTS SOFTLY]

119
00:06:54,767 --> 00:06:57,733
[ANGSTY MUSIC PLAYING]

120
00:06:57,733 --> 00:06:59,100
[GRUNTS]

121
00:06:59,100 --> 00:07:02,300
- What happened?
- They hit me! The agent!

122
00:07:02,300 --> 00:07:04,100
You can sue them.
You have a lawyer, right?

123
00:07:04,100 --> 00:07:07,200
I will call my lawyer!
I will file a case!

124
00:07:07,200 --> 00:07:09,200
Why did that NCIA agent
hit you?!

125
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:11,500
They forced me to confess!

126
00:07:11,500 --> 00:07:12,600
What did you say?

127
00:07:12,600 --> 00:07:16,067
No! I didn't talk.
I said nothing!

128
00:07:16,100 --> 00:07:20,000
[ANGSTY MUSIC CONTINUES]

129
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:23,400
I hate that lady agent!

130
00:07:23,400 --> 00:07:26,533
I really hate her!

131
00:07:26,533 --> 00:07:29,933
<i>The NCIA will use you
against me, Mr. Chan.</i>

132
00:07:29,933 --> 00:07:34,867
<i>I'll deal with you
before you bring me down.</i>

133
00:07:41,800 --> 00:07:48,300
- [PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]
- "PREVENTIVE SUSPENSION ORDER"

134
00:07:50,167 --> 00:07:55,567
This hurts me
because you're good at this.

135
00:07:55,567 --> 00:08:01,067
Lately, you've made
mistake after mistake.

136
00:08:01,067 --> 00:08:02,867
Your decisions...

137
00:08:02,867 --> 00:08:04,400
What?

138
00:08:04,400 --> 00:08:07,567
Is something going on at home?

139
00:08:07,567 --> 00:08:10,133
Are you just looking
for trouble?

140
00:08:10,133 --> 00:08:13,267
I'm telling you, Sam,
this is work!

141
00:08:15,067 --> 00:08:17,567
I just knew we could solve
this case.

142
00:08:17,567 --> 00:08:19,800
Yes, I know.
Your intentions are good.

143
00:08:19,800 --> 00:08:23,900
But we enforce the law.

144
00:08:23,933 --> 00:08:25,633
If we break it,

145
00:08:25,633 --> 00:08:29,700
we're no different from
the criminals we catch.

146
00:08:29,700 --> 00:08:36,567
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

147
00:08:43,233 --> 00:08:47,600
Admin put you on
preventive suspension.

148
00:08:47,600 --> 00:08:50,633
Honestly, it's for the best.

149
00:08:50,633 --> 00:08:55,933
You're way too emotionally
involved in this case.

150
00:08:55,967 --> 00:09:01,967
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

151
00:09:01,967 --> 00:09:03,167
Sign it.

152
00:09:03,167 --> 00:09:10,467
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

153
00:09:12,967 --> 00:09:17,400
Leave your badge and gun
before you go.

154
00:09:17,400 --> 00:09:24,233
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

155
00:09:39,900 --> 00:09:41,233
You may go.

156
00:09:41,233 --> 00:09:47,733
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

157
00:09:47,733 --> 00:09:49,167
Samantha...

158
00:09:52,600 --> 00:09:55,833
Use this time to reflect.

159
00:09:55,833 --> 00:09:59,133
It'll help you become
a better agent.

160
00:10:01,100 --> 00:10:03,200
I know you will find your way.

161
00:10:03,200 --> 00:10:10,067
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

162
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:20,133
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

163
00:10:20,133 --> 00:10:20,933
Oh!

164
00:10:21,833 --> 00:10:23,100
Where's your badge?

165
00:10:24,200 --> 00:10:25,933
And your gun?

166
00:10:25,933 --> 00:10:27,000
[SCOFFS]

167
00:10:28,033 --> 00:10:29,800
Have you been removed
from duty?

168
00:10:31,633 --> 00:10:33,900
Well-deserved!

169
00:10:38,067 --> 00:10:39,300
It's just a suspension.

170
00:10:39,300 --> 00:10:41,533
You're too full
of yourself, huh?

171
00:10:43,967 --> 00:10:47,467
Typical nepo baby.

172
00:10:48,900 --> 00:10:53,167
You think, because of
the name you carry,

173
00:10:53,167 --> 00:10:58,233
you can do whatever you want
without repercussions?

174
00:10:59,800 --> 00:11:01,300
[SNICKERS]

175
00:11:01,300 --> 00:11:03,467
Feeling entitled much?

176
00:11:04,267 --> 00:11:06,200
I just did what
I thought was right.

177
00:11:06,200 --> 00:11:07,500
No.

178
00:11:07,500 --> 00:11:11,933
You did as you pleased.

179
00:11:14,467 --> 00:11:16,133
You're such a show-off.

180
00:11:16,833 --> 00:11:18,600
You're not a hero, Sam.

181
00:11:21,033 --> 00:11:27,633
You are the biggest liability
of NCIA.

182
00:11:27,633 --> 00:11:34,333
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

183
00:11:38,467 --> 00:11:40,233
What?

184
00:11:42,767 --> 00:11:44,733
Are you going to hit me too?

185
00:11:45,767 --> 00:11:46,867
Hm?

186
00:11:46,867 --> 00:11:53,633
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

187
00:12:12,600 --> 00:12:13,933
[SIGHS DEEPLY]

188
00:12:18,067 --> 00:12:19,333
[GUN COCKS]

189
00:12:23,433 --> 00:12:25,800
[GLASS CLINK]

190
00:12:30,633 --> 00:12:32,200
Is your wound healed?

191
00:12:33,433 --> 00:12:34,700
I'm fine, Ma.

192
00:12:36,167 --> 00:12:38,100
We can't waste time.

193
00:12:39,167 --> 00:12:41,133
We need to act now.

194
00:12:41,133 --> 00:12:42,433
[HUFFS]

195
00:12:42,433 --> 00:12:46,133
So, what are you planning to do?

196
00:12:46,133 --> 00:12:48,700
If I can't silence Mr. Chan...

197
00:12:49,667 --> 00:12:52,233
I'll just take down
Samantha Jacinto.

198
00:12:53,567 --> 00:12:55,967
Revenge isn't what
we need right now.

199
00:12:59,467 --> 00:13:00,867
Then what?

200
00:13:00,867 --> 00:13:02,033
Patience.

201
00:13:03,400 --> 00:13:04,533
We wait.

202
00:13:05,200 --> 00:13:08,167
But, Ma, I can't just sit here
and do nothing

203
00:13:08,167 --> 00:13:10,367
while Samantha Jacinto
is out there.

204
00:13:11,100 --> 00:13:15,133
He sent Victor to jail
and shot me!

205
00:13:15,133 --> 00:13:17,233
She messed with our family,

206
00:13:17,233 --> 00:13:19,100
and I'll make her pay for it.

207
00:13:20,533 --> 00:13:24,867
I know that anger is
the flame that keeps you going.

208
00:13:25,933 --> 00:13:28,133
But fire can be destructive.

209
00:13:29,033 --> 00:13:33,967
Don't let the same flames
burn you.

210
00:13:33,967 --> 00:13:40,800
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

211
00:13:41,933 --> 00:13:43,633
You think Sir Seb
will get in trouble too?

212
00:13:43,633 --> 00:13:46,767
He was also there
when Sam interrogated Mr. Chan.

213
00:13:46,767 --> 00:13:49,033
Why are you more concerned
about Sir Seb?

214
00:13:49,033 --> 00:13:51,033
Sam's the one who was
summoned by the director.

215
00:13:51,033 --> 00:13:54,433
What now?
Sir Delgado's furious.

216
00:13:54,433 --> 00:13:58,133
I think anyone would be angry
with what Ma'am Sam did.

217
00:13:58,167 --> 00:14:02,167
I wasn't expecting
Sam would punch Mr. Chan.

218
00:14:02,167 --> 00:14:04,267
- Is there anyone who did?
- And because of that...

219
00:14:04,267 --> 00:14:06,267
...she might actually
face suspension.

220
00:14:06,267 --> 00:14:10,733
Suspended or not,
our problem remains.

221
00:14:12,533 --> 00:14:15,700
- What?
- Mr. Chan still won't squeak!

222
00:14:15,700 --> 00:14:17,633
And the gold bars
are still missing.

223
00:14:17,633 --> 00:14:20,233
I'm more worried
about Zafra's men.

224
00:14:20,233 --> 00:14:21,733
When we faced them last night,

225
00:14:21,733 --> 00:14:24,000
we got a taste
of how dangerous they are.

226
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:26,700
What if they get back at us?
At Sam?

227
00:14:26,700 --> 00:14:33,300
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

228
00:14:33,833 --> 00:14:37,233
The NCIA has arrested Mr. Chan.

229
00:14:37,233 --> 00:14:38,200
Attorney.

230
00:14:39,133 --> 00:14:42,833
Make sure to keep
his mouth shut.

231
00:14:42,833 --> 00:14:46,600
If he incriminates Victor,
my son will rot in jail.

232
00:14:47,533 --> 00:14:51,233
That won't be easy, ma'am.
He's in the custody of NCIA.

233
00:14:51,233 --> 00:14:53,467
Let's just attack the NCIA!

234
00:14:53,467 --> 00:14:54,600
Lucas...

235
00:14:55,533 --> 00:14:58,133
What did I tell you about
being patient?

236
00:14:58,133 --> 00:15:00,633
Attacking the NCIA now

237
00:15:00,633 --> 00:15:04,033
is the same as throwing away
all our businesses.

238
00:15:05,467 --> 00:15:10,000
Attorney, is there no other way
to get Victor out?

239
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:12,333
Name your price.
We will pay you.

240
00:15:12,333 --> 00:15:14,100
Just get Victor out.

241
00:15:15,033 --> 00:15:17,467
There's still another way.

242
00:15:18,333 --> 00:15:21,600
We haven't used
all our cards yet.

243
00:15:21,600 --> 00:15:23,967
I have another ace up my sleeve.

244
00:15:25,700 --> 00:15:30,867
We just have to think carefully
when we're going to drop it.

245
00:15:31,933 --> 00:15:34,667
Nothing good may have come out
of your talk with Ricardo...

246
00:15:35,633 --> 00:15:38,700
...and we couldn't stop
Mr. Chan.

247
00:15:39,633 --> 00:15:41,500
But we can still do something.

248
00:15:42,333 --> 00:15:45,767
There's one more way.

249
00:15:45,767 --> 00:15:48,000
But it may be our last recourse.

250
00:15:48,767 --> 00:15:50,033
What is it?

251
00:15:50,033 --> 00:15:51,633
[DEBORAH] Attorney.

252
00:15:51,633 --> 00:15:56,100
May we go to the NCIA
to visit our son?

253
00:15:57,033 --> 00:15:58,933
Is there any risk?

254
00:15:58,933 --> 00:16:03,167
At the moment, only Victor
has a warrant against him.

255
00:16:03,167 --> 00:16:06,833
You and Sir Mariano
aren't facing any pending cases.

256
00:16:06,833 --> 00:16:10,700
They can't arrest you
for being his parents.

257
00:16:12,933 --> 00:16:14,900
We're going to the NCIA?

258
00:16:16,233 --> 00:16:17,300
Why not?

259
00:16:18,900 --> 00:16:22,000
It just goes to show that we
have nothing to hide

260
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:26,067
and we will cooperate
with them if necessary.

261
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:30,733
It's time to visit our son.

262
00:16:30,733 --> 00:16:37,767
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

263
00:16:46,800 --> 00:16:48,167
Mister Elton!

264
00:16:48,167 --> 00:16:49,500
- Mister Elton!
- Yeah!

265
00:16:49,500 --> 00:16:51,400
- Good morning!
- My idol! My idol!

266
00:16:51,400 --> 00:16:53,000
- My idol!
- Our idol!

267
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:54,700
What's nice about the morning?

268
00:16:54,700 --> 00:16:56,467
- So grumpy!
- Geez, you're grumpy today.

269
00:16:56,467 --> 00:16:58,133
You're all being a pain
this early.

270
00:16:58,133 --> 00:16:59,633
[BONG] Mister Elton...

271
00:16:59,633 --> 00:17:01,500
Is Gabo home?
Has he arrived yet?

272
00:17:01,500 --> 00:17:03,233
I've been waiting for him
since last night,

273
00:17:03,233 --> 00:17:05,200
- and he's still not around!
- Okay, don't shout.

274
00:17:05,200 --> 00:17:07,733
Now, don't take your anger
out on us, Mister Elton!

275
00:17:07,733 --> 00:17:09,233
We can't ask you a question?

276
00:17:09,233 --> 00:17:11,267
- He's too worked up.
- You've really changed!

277
00:17:11,267 --> 00:17:13,500
- [LAUGHTER]
- [LIVELY MUSIC PLAYING]

278
00:17:13,500 --> 00:17:16,433
- He seems hot-headed today.
- Well, what's new?

279
00:17:16,467 --> 00:17:18,667
Tell me. Who wouldn't be?

280
00:17:19,067 --> 00:17:21,433
The seaman's coming today
to get his bike.

281
00:17:21,433 --> 00:17:23,700
- [TEKLA] Look what you've done!
- Well, that explains it.

282
00:17:23,700 --> 00:17:26,067
That's such a simple problem,
Mister Elton.

283
00:17:26,067 --> 00:17:29,200
If he gets here first,
just ask him to wait.

284
00:17:29,200 --> 00:17:30,767
- To be more patient.
- Right.

285
00:17:30,767 --> 00:17:32,067
[IPE] With an easy fix, too.

286
00:17:32,067 --> 00:17:34,000
- Just entertain him!
- [TEKLA, BONG] Yeah!

287
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:36,067
You're a good dancer.
Show it off!

288
00:17:36,067 --> 00:17:39,067
[BINOY] And he's a singer, too!
His voice is amazing!

289
00:17:39,067 --> 00:17:40,400
- You serious?
- Yeah!

290
00:17:40,400 --> 00:17:41,767
Here's a song idea,

291
00:17:41,767 --> 00:17:45,067
since you look like both
the singer and the composer.

292
00:17:45,067 --> 00:17:46,767
- [SINGS]<i> Let's groove...
</i>- Oh!

293
00:17:46,767 --> 00:17:50,433
[ALL SINGING]<i> The lucky seven
</i> The lucky seven

294
00:17:50,467 --> 00:17:52,067
[BINOY] He's about to smile!

295
00:17:52,067 --> 00:17:53,200
[LAUGHTER]

296
00:17:53,200 --> 00:17:56,133
What was that?
You got the dance craze wrong!

297
00:17:56,700 --> 00:17:58,467
It's the lucky eight!

298
00:17:58,467 --> 00:18:00,067
- Oh, okay...
- [DABOY] Like this?

299
00:18:00,067 --> 00:18:01,200
Look at me!

300
00:18:01,200 --> 00:18:04,167
- Whoa, whoa!
- Yeah!

301
00:18:04,167 --> 00:18:06,400
- [LAUGHTER]
- [MAMENG] Hey, careful now.

302
00:18:06,400 --> 00:18:08,200
[TEKLA] Turns out,
you're the solution.

303
00:18:08,200 --> 00:18:09,667
[BETCHAY] Psst! Hey, Dante!

304
00:18:09,667 --> 00:18:11,833
Do a better job
helping him along!

305
00:18:12,567 --> 00:18:13,833
Hey, Mister Rudy!

306
00:18:13,833 --> 00:18:15,700
So you're out
of the hospital already.

307
00:18:15,700 --> 00:18:16,867
Take a shot!

308
00:18:17,400 --> 00:18:19,867
- Seriously? A drink?
- Glad you're better now, Rudy.

309
00:18:19,867 --> 00:18:21,767
Thanks for your concern.

310
00:18:21,800 --> 00:18:24,100
He's from Ginintuang Lupa!

311
00:18:24,100 --> 00:18:25,567
He's tough like a weed!

312
00:18:25,567 --> 00:18:27,533
Nothing can kill him
that easily!

313
00:18:27,533 --> 00:18:29,333
Slow down now, Miss Diday.

314
00:18:29,333 --> 00:18:33,333
All I'm saying is, the pandemic
didn't take any of us down.

315
00:18:33,333 --> 00:18:35,700
If a virus couldn't,
neither can a bullet!

316
00:18:35,700 --> 00:18:37,300
[MAMENG] You have a point there.

317
00:18:37,300 --> 00:18:40,633
Garbage smell made us
strong enough, didn't it?

318
00:18:40,633 --> 00:18:42,333
- Correct!
- Alright, that's enough.

319
00:18:42,333 --> 00:18:44,433
Rudy is going
to get some rest, okay?

320
00:18:44,433 --> 00:18:45,733
Kiss him, Betchay.

321
00:18:45,733 --> 00:18:47,867
- We'll head inside now.
- All the kisses.

322
00:18:47,867 --> 00:18:48,867
Hey!

323
00:18:48,867 --> 00:18:50,233
- Betchay!
- It's Mister Rudy!

324
00:18:50,233 --> 00:18:51,267
Mister Rudy!

325
00:18:51,267 --> 00:18:53,300
- Mister Rudy!
- Mister Rudy!

326
00:18:53,300 --> 00:18:55,100
- Mister Rudy!
- [CHUCKLES] He's back!

327
00:18:55,133 --> 00:18:57,000
- Make way!
- There he goes!

328
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:59,000
- Rudy, I missed you!
- Oh, Elton...

329
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:00,533
- We all did.
- No, no!

330
00:19:00,533 --> 00:19:01,900
- Mind his wound!
- Hey!

331
00:19:01,900 --> 00:19:05,833
Come on now, Elton.
He just had surgery, remember?

332
00:19:05,833 --> 00:19:07,700
Sorry, I just missed him.

333
00:19:07,700 --> 00:19:09,167
You saw the sling, right?

334
00:19:09,167 --> 00:19:11,633
What's up, Mister Rudy?
Are you okay?

335
00:19:11,633 --> 00:19:13,867
- Yes, I'm okay.
- [IPE] Hang on, Mister Rudy.

336
00:19:13,867 --> 00:19:16,167
Isn't Gabo supposed to be
with you? Where is he?

337
00:19:16,167 --> 00:19:18,900
Oh, he didn't come with us.
He took the bike.

338
00:19:19,267 --> 00:19:21,500
[DANTE]
He's probably on his way now.

339
00:19:21,500 --> 00:19:23,400
Wait a second.
He's not yet here?

340
00:19:23,400 --> 00:19:24,667
He left before us.

341
00:19:25,133 --> 00:19:26,333
Not yet.

342
00:19:26,333 --> 00:19:28,333
Anyway, we're happy
that you're finally discharged.

343
00:19:28,367 --> 00:19:32,033
If you only knew the things
Gabo went through.

344
00:19:32,033 --> 00:19:33,267
- Yup.
- [BETCHAY] Why?

345
00:19:33,267 --> 00:19:34,867
What did he do this time?

346
00:19:34,867 --> 00:19:37,433
Oh, there's too many
to mention, Miss Betchay.

347
00:19:37,433 --> 00:19:38,900
But that doesn't matter anymore.

348
00:19:38,900 --> 00:19:41,533
What matter is that
Mister Rudy is finally home!

349
00:19:41,533 --> 00:19:43,767
- [SQUEALS] Yay!
- Exactly. It's important.

350
00:19:43,767 --> 00:19:46,233
[BETCHAY] Alright, then.
We're going inside now

351
00:19:46,233 --> 00:19:48,400
- so Rudy can get some rest.
- Let's let him recover.

352
00:19:48,400 --> 00:19:50,167
- Let's drink later!
- We want to come too!

353
00:19:50,167 --> 00:19:51,633
[BINOY]
Let's chill at your place!

354
00:19:51,633 --> 00:19:54,000
- So stubborn.
- Give him space for now.

355
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:57,033
- Drinking session later.
- Absolutely not.

356
00:19:57,033 --> 00:20:00,033
[SINGING]
<i> Let's groove the lucky seven</i>

357
00:20:00,033 --> 00:20:02,267
[MUSIC FADING]

358
00:20:02,300 --> 00:20:04,100
- [HORN HONKING IN DISTANCE]
- [INDISTINCT CROWD CHATTER]

359
00:20:06,400 --> 00:20:08,600
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

360
00:20:08,600 --> 00:20:11,900
[SALVADOR] The people here
are suffering terribly.

361
00:20:11,900 --> 00:20:13,300
What's happening?

362
00:20:13,300 --> 00:20:17,033
I really need
to break a story here.

363
00:20:18,067 --> 00:20:20,000
My heart breaks for them.

364
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:26,267
Politicians keep stealing
instead of helping.

365
00:20:26,267 --> 00:20:28,167
I'll give this my absolute best.

366
00:20:28,167 --> 00:20:31,500
I'll pour everything
into this program

367
00:20:31,500 --> 00:20:33,700
so I can help more people.

368
00:20:34,033 --> 00:20:35,200
Those poor people!

369
00:20:35,633 --> 00:20:36,767
My goodness.

370
00:20:36,767 --> 00:20:39,433
[ENGINE REVVING]

371
00:20:39,433 --> 00:20:46,400
[MUSIC BECOMES SUSPENSEFUL]

372
00:20:47,200 --> 00:20:48,333
[MOTORCYCLE ENGINE TURNS ON]

373
00:20:49,967 --> 00:20:55,633
[MOTORCYCLE ENGINES REVVING]

374
00:21:01,200 --> 00:21:07,467
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

375
00:21:07,467 --> 00:21:10,000
"Fearless...
Fearless reporting."

376
00:21:11,033 --> 00:21:12,633
"Endless digging."

377
00:21:13,433 --> 00:21:16,933
"Fearless reporting.
Endless digging."

378
00:21:17,600 --> 00:21:19,700
I need to sound relentless.
Hang on.

379
00:21:19,700 --> 00:21:21,300
[REVVING CONTINUES]

380
00:21:21,300 --> 00:21:24,000
[SHOUTS] "Fearless reporting!
Endless digging!"

381
00:21:25,033 --> 00:21:29,167
"Just the truth
with Salvador Manalo!"

382
00:21:29,167 --> 00:21:30,267
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

383
00:21:30,267 --> 00:21:31,733
"Fearless reporting!

384
00:21:31,733 --> 00:21:33,000
Endless digging!"

385
00:21:33,400 --> 00:21:37,367
"Just the truth
with Salvador Manalo!"

386
00:21:44,867 --> 00:21:51,767
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

387
00:21:51,767 --> 00:21:55,400
[REVVING CONTINUES]

388
00:21:58,333 --> 00:22:00,133
[FIRE CRACKLING]

389
00:22:02,667 --> 00:22:04,067
[WATER SPLASHING]

390
00:22:04,067 --> 00:22:06,067
- Stop the car!
- Pull over!

391
00:22:06,067 --> 00:22:07,700
[TIRES SCREECH]

392
00:22:07,700 --> 00:22:09,033
Out of the car!

393
00:22:09,033 --> 00:22:10,000
[SALVADOR] Boss!

394
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:11,367
What's going on, boss?

395
00:22:11,367 --> 00:22:13,167
- What did I do?
- You talk too much!

396
00:22:13,167 --> 00:22:15,467
I won't fight back! I promise!

397
00:22:15,500 --> 00:22:17,167
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [GROANING]

398
00:22:18,000 --> 00:22:19,467
- Get up!
- I won't fight back!

399
00:22:19,467 --> 00:22:23,767
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [GROANING]

400
00:22:23,767 --> 00:22:24,900
[ENGINE ROARING]

401
00:22:24,900 --> 00:22:27,467
[SALVADOR] I won't fight back!
No, no, no!

402
00:22:28,400 --> 00:22:29,400
Hey!

403
00:22:29,900 --> 00:22:32,167
[ENGINE REVVING]

404
00:22:32,167 --> 00:22:33,567
- Hey!
- Whoa!

405
00:22:33,567 --> 00:22:35,000
[BODIES THUD]

406
00:22:35,833 --> 00:22:36,767
[HEAVY THUD]

407
00:22:37,200 --> 00:22:38,200
[MOTORCYCLE CLATTERS]

408
00:22:38,200 --> 00:22:44,267
[THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING]

409
00:22:44,267 --> 00:22:45,200
[WHIMPERS]

410
00:22:46,400 --> 00:22:47,867
[BRASS KNUCKLES
SLICING THROUGH AIR]

411
00:22:54,500 --> 00:22:56,400
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

412
00:22:56,400 --> 00:22:58,500
- [KICK LANDS]
- [KNIFE SWISHING]

413
00:22:58,500 --> 00:23:00,800
- [BLOWS LAND]
- [MAN GROANS] Agh!

414
00:23:00,800 --> 00:23:02,400
- [KICKS LANDS]
- [MAN GROANS] Agh!

415
00:23:02,400 --> 00:23:03,367
[BLOW LANDS]

416
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:04,933
[BODY THUDS]

417
00:23:04,933 --> 00:23:06,233
[KNIFE SWISHING]

418
00:23:06,233 --> 00:23:08,200
- [BLOWS LAND]
- [MAN GROANS] Agh!

419
00:23:08,200 --> 00:23:10,000
- [KNIFE CLINKS]
- [MAN GROANS] Agh!

420
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:13,500
[BLOWS LANDS]

421
00:23:13,500 --> 00:23:14,900
- [BODY THUDS]
- [KICK LANDS]

422
00:23:16,200 --> 00:23:17,400
[KICK LANDS]

423
00:23:17,400 --> 00:23:18,467
[WATER SPLASHES]

424
00:23:20,300 --> 00:23:21,467
[GRUNTS] Argh!

425
00:23:22,133 --> 00:23:23,100
[BLOW LANDS]

426
00:23:24,133 --> 00:23:25,633
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [MAN GROANS] Agh!

427
00:23:25,633 --> 00:23:27,633
- [KICKS LAND]
- [MAN GROANS] Agh!

428
00:23:27,633 --> 00:23:29,000
- [BLOWS LAND]
- [MAN GROANS] Agh!

429
00:23:31,133 --> 00:23:32,333
[KICK LANDS]

430
00:23:32,333 --> 00:23:33,367
[BODY THUDS]

431
00:23:33,367 --> 00:23:36,400
[TENSE MUSIC FADES]

432
00:23:39,533 --> 00:23:40,633
[WHIMPERS]

433
00:23:40,633 --> 00:23:45,233
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

434
00:23:45,233 --> 00:23:46,400
What's your name?

435
00:23:47,533 --> 00:23:49,233
I'm Salvador Manalo.

436
00:23:50,133 --> 00:23:53,300
I'm a reporter
at M-Manila Telebalita.

437
00:23:55,833 --> 00:23:56,967
You can stand up now.

438
00:24:04,333 --> 00:24:05,567
Why do they want to kill you?

439
00:24:06,200 --> 00:24:07,367
I have no idea.

440
00:24:08,400 --> 00:24:11,067
They were robbing me.
Then they wanted to kill me too.

441
00:24:12,900 --> 00:24:15,267
You better go now.

442
00:24:16,233 --> 00:24:17,467
They'll wake up soon.

443
00:24:18,333 --> 00:24:19,767
A-Aren't you going to hurt me?

444
00:24:21,800 --> 00:24:22,967
I'm not going to hurt you.

445
00:24:25,100 --> 00:24:26,000
Come on, leave.

446
00:24:26,633 --> 00:24:27,800
Thank you, thank you.

447
00:24:29,533 --> 00:24:30,800
What's your name?

448
00:24:34,833 --> 00:24:35,867
Gabo.

449
00:24:35,867 --> 00:24:41,167
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

450
00:24:41,167 --> 00:24:42,400
Gabo! Gabo! Gabo!

451
00:24:43,133 --> 00:24:44,233
Hold on.

452
00:24:45,933 --> 00:24:49,033
Looks like your motorcycle
broke down because of me.

453
00:24:50,867 --> 00:24:52,433
Gabo.

454
00:24:52,433 --> 00:24:53,433
Here.

455
00:24:56,800 --> 00:24:59,000
P-Please take this, Gabo.

456
00:24:59,000 --> 00:25:00,333
To cover the cost of repair.

457
00:25:03,800 --> 00:25:05,200
Don't worry about it.

458
00:25:05,200 --> 00:25:06,600
Gabo, this is not even enough.

459
00:25:06,600 --> 00:25:08,600
This is not even enough
for what you did for me.

460
00:25:08,600 --> 00:25:09,767
You saved my life.

461
00:25:11,300 --> 00:25:12,267
Gabo.

462
00:25:13,133 --> 00:25:14,667
Come on. Take it.

463
00:25:15,633 --> 00:25:16,800
I hope that helps.

464
00:25:17,800 --> 00:25:19,567
One day I'll be able
to help you too.

465
00:25:21,933 --> 00:25:23,067
Thank you so much.

466
00:25:25,100 --> 00:25:26,533
I really need this.

467
00:25:26,533 --> 00:25:27,967
That's not even enough
for what you've done.

468
00:25:31,300 --> 00:25:32,900
Okay. Be careful.

469
00:25:37,167 --> 00:25:43,633
- [MOTORCYCLE ENGINE REVVING]
- [TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

470
00:25:43,633 --> 00:25:47,367
<i>You want to take revenge
because of my reports on you.</i>

471
00:25:47,367 --> 00:25:49,467
<i>Only one person
did that?! Stupid!</i>

472
00:25:49,467 --> 00:25:53,067
<i>I'm making your jobs harder,
aren't I?!</i>

473
00:25:53,067 --> 00:25:55,800
<i>If you've just followed
what I've told you,</i>

474
00:25:55,800 --> 00:25:57,167
<i> they wouldn't have failed!</i>

475
00:25:57,167 --> 00:25:58,367
<i> Whose order was it to kill me?</i>

476
00:25:58,367 --> 00:26:00,467
<i>Was it your men?
Did you ask them?</i>

477
00:26:00,467 --> 00:26:03,567
With every mistake
he's trying to make right...

478
00:26:03,567 --> 00:26:04,700
<i>What happened
to the motorcycle?!</i>

479
00:26:04,700 --> 00:26:06,367
The owner will pick it up today!

480
00:26:06,367 --> 00:26:07,567
<i> You just brought problems!</i>

481
00:26:07,567 --> 00:26:10,267
... a hitch
is waiting to happen.

482
00:26:10,300 --> 00:26:12,500
<i>You had it for a long time!
You're delaying the pickup day!</i>

483
00:26:12,500 --> 00:26:14,033
<i> It just had a little scratch.</i>

484
00:26:14,033 --> 00:26:15,500
<i> A scratch?! It looks ruined!</i>

485
00:26:15,500 --> 00:26:17,333
<i>The next time I come back,
I should be getting it.</i>

486
00:26:17,333 --> 00:26:19,400
<i>Or else we'll see each other
in court.</i>

487
00:26:19,400 --> 00:26:20,833
I'll go back to Ginintuang Lupa.

488
00:26:20,833 --> 00:26:23,200
<i> The man who saved Salvador</i>

489
00:26:23,200 --> 00:26:26,400
<i>is the reason
why we have this problem!</i>

490
00:26:26,400 --> 00:26:28,133
<i> Find out who he is.</i>

491
00:26:28,133 --> 00:26:30,267
<i>I'll surely do.
I'll make him pay.</i>
